From a075dfa1f792a1193d03af1e792830010d59d90a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joris-sta <joris-sta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:44:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ptq1: Pascal DP4A matmul kernels and quantize fusion for
 ternary weights

MMQ: PTQ1_0 (1.75-bit ternary) prefill entries in the sm_61 DP4A config
lift the shared Q8-SRAM tile path to ternary: each weight block decodes
once and lands in the existing Q8 shared tile, so every model carrying
this packing gets the stock DP4A multiply without a bespoke dot kernel.
Gated by GGML_CUDA_PTQ1_PASCAL_MMQ=auto|off|on (on for cc==610).

GEMV/MMVQ: a dedicated dense PTQ1-only decode path for SM 6.1
(mmvq-ptq1-pascal.cuh) reuses one quantized Q8 activation row across
four PTQ1 output rows per block, and fuses quantization with the signed
FWHT input rotation when the graph provides one; sign vectors and packed
code are unpacked on the fly. Gated by GGML_CUDA_PTQ1_PASCAL_GEMV,
auto-selected only for supported dense shapes (single GPU, no MoE,
ne11<=4, widths-multiple-of-128); unsupported batches, splits and
fusions keep the established Q8 MMVQ contract. Supported tile geometry
is centralized in ptq1-pascal-layout.cuh.

Dedicated device test test-ptq1-pascal (cuda test wheel, SKIP on
non-CUDA) validates the PTQ1 decode, quantize fusion and tile selection
against reference arithmetic.
